          "objective": "Use approved-repository-analysis to review the supplied implementation for correctness bugs preventing shipping, with cited evidence.",
          "report_markdown": "# Repository analysis\n\n## Investigation objective\nUse approved-repository-analysis to review the supplied implementation for correctness bugs preventing shipping, with cited evidence.\n\n## Approved source scope\nSource c2e669ae-e5b4-4b53-8038-3819038d6121 (digest 46736c0dbfa64356e847b2fecc8371b11fc7d75f29d6e4895141ab41f654d86b).\nFiles supplied to the model: README.md, mean.py.\nOmitted: none.\nThis analysis covers only those files, not the whole repository.\n\n## Model summary (model assessment, not verified)\nmean.py has a shipping-blocking correctness bug: denominator is len+1 instead of len, contradicting README spec.\n\n## Findings whose citations exist in the captured files\n\n### F1-off-by-one-denomin: Off-by-one denominator in mean prevents correct average\nModel-assessed severity: high; category: correctness.\nmean divides by len(values)+1 instead of len(values), so it never returns the arithmetic mean. E.g. mean([2,4]) returns 2.0 instead of 3.0. This blocks shipping.\nEvidence:\n- mean.py:1-2 (quote_matches)\n- mean.py:2-2 (quote_matches)\n- README.md:2-2 (quote_matches)\nUncertainty: None on formula mismatch; empty-list behavior not shown in supplied files.\nSuggested verification: Run mean([2,4]) and check equals 3; inspect edge cases.\n\n## Unsupported hypotheses (a citation did not match the captured files)\nNone.\n\n## Unresolved questions\n- Expected behavior for empty input is not defined in supplied files.\n\n## Validation status\nCitation existence: 1 of 1 findings have citations that match the captured files.\nA matching citation shows the cited lines exist. It does not show the model is right.\nIndependent verification: none performed. Semantic status: unverified.",
